Package: pistomp-audio
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: pistomp <pistomp@example.com>
Depends: rtirq-init, python3, alsa-utils
Description: Realtime audio IRQ tuning and PCM bind repair for pi-Stomp
 Raises the i2s audio DMA interrupt threads to SCHED_FIFO 90 so they sit
 above jackd. On Pi 3/4 the shipped resolver derives the audio IRQs from
 the device topology (name matching cannot: every bcm2835 DMA channel
 shares the label "DMA IRQ"); on Pi 5 it defers to rtirq with the packaged
 config.
 .
 Also repairs a sound card that bound without its dmaengine platform
 component, which makes every open() of the PCM return EINVAL with nothing
 in the kernel log. ASoC binds the platform half of a DAI link with no
 deferred probe, and bcm2835-i2s registers its CPU DAI before that
 platform, so a machine driver matching by of_node can bind to the wrong
 component. OTA upgrades take effect at the next boot.
